WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.051
Shine a torch straight down on a leaning stick. It makes a shadow on the floor. The angle between a line and a plane is the angle between the line and its shadow. The shadow is called the projection.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:27.725
Drop a vertical from the top end of the line to the plane. Its foot is the point directly below. Join the foot to the other end. The line, projection and vertical make a right-angled triangle.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:37.050
In a right pyramid, the line from the vertex to the centre of the base is vertical. So the centre is the foot. For edge E A, the projection is A M.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:44.982
This type asks for the angle between a line and a plane. Find the foot, draw the projection, then use trigonometry.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:55.191
Step one: find the point on the plane directly below the top of the line. Step two: join it to the other end.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:02.752
Step three: find the height and the projection. Step four: use tan, sin or cos to find the angle.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.054
The trap is measuring from a base edge, instead of from the projection.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:25.192
November twenty twenty four. Figure one shows a right prism A B C D E F, with a triangular cross section C D E. The measurements are on the card. Find the angle between the line F D and the plane D C B A. Six marks.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:34.256
Here is Figure one, redrawn. F B is a vertical edge, so F is directly above B. B is the foot of the line F D.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:41.491
Step two: the projection of F D is B D. So we need angle F D B, in the right-angled triangle F B D.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:53.453
Step three: the end triangle. F B is fifteen sine forty, nine point six four two. D C is fifteen cosine forty, eleven point four nine one.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:02:03.938
Step four: B D is the base diagonal. D C is eleven point four nine one and C B is twenty. So B D is twenty three point zero six six.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:15.600
Step five: tan of angle F D B is height over projection: nine point six four two over twenty three point zero six six. The angle is twenty two point seven degrees.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:25.171
A tempting route measures from the base edge D A. That gives thirty six point nine degrees. But D A is not the shadow of F D.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:35.248
So the angle between F D and the plane is twenty two point seven degrees, to one decimal place. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:46.356
A common mistake is turning the tan ratio upside down. Projection over height gives sixty seven point three degrees, which is far too big.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:59.711
Now you try, from November twenty twenty. Find the angle between A E and the base, to one decimal place. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:10.197
The foot of E is M, the centre. So the projection of A E is A M. The base diagonal is twenty, so A M is ten.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:18.516
In triangle E M A, tan of the angle is height over projection, fourteen over ten. The angle is fifty four point five degrees.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:27.734
The common wrong answer uses the whole diagonal, twenty, as the projection. That gives thirty five degrees. The shadow stops at the centre M.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.697
Remember: find the foot, join it to make the projection, then use tan, sin or cos.
